        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(shared): consolidate provider loaders and enforce lazy runtime helpers",
        "body": "Related: #98748\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nResolves the final provider and utility portion of a maintainability problem where bundled plugins and provider adapters repeatedly implement their own dynamic-import promise caches.\r\n\r\nThe shared foundation and core leaf batches are already merged:\r\n\r\n- #99261 — lazy runtime loader foundation\r\n- #99278 — core leaf lazy loaders\r\n\r\nThe gateway and channel batches must land before this PR can enforce the repository-wide manual-memoizer guard.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nMigrates the remaining provider and utility plugin loaders to the public `openclaw/plugin-sdk/lazy-runtime` helper while preserving each existing sticky-rejection, retry, reset, and inspection contract. The memory-lancedb provider path retains retry-after-failure behavior; other runtime imports retain sticky rejection caching. The dynamic-import wart checker also gains a focused enforcement mode for hand-written `??=` import memoizers.\r\n\r\nThis PR remains draft while the gateway and channel batches are outstanding. The enforcement command is expected to fail against the current stacked state because those unmerged batches still own the remaining memoizers; this PR does not broaden allowlists or hide them.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nNo intended user-visible behavior change. Maintainers get one canonical lazy runtime loader across provider and utility plugins, plus a final repository guard that becomes green once the preceding gateway and channel batches land.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- Exact scope: 37 files, `+247/-347`; no paths outside the final provider/utility/enforcement batch.\r\n- Focused provider/plugin proof: 11 Vitest shards passed, covering 29 test files and 894 tests.\r\n- Browser sticky-rejection follow-up: 2 files, 23 tests passed after removing rejection eviction found by autoreview.\r\n- Existing unrelated failure: `extensions/moonshot/src/kimi-web-search-provider.test.ts` has one base-URL assertion failure; it reproduces with `extensions/moonshot/src/kimi-web-search-provider.ts` restored to current `origin/main`, so this PR does not change that behavior.\r\n- Format: `oxfmt --check` passed on all 37 owned files.\r\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox `tbx_01kwjsd175zx3727rf4v898cde`: `check:changed` passed, including extension production/test typechecks, extension and script lint, runtime sidecar loader checks, and 0 runtime import cycles.\r\n- Testbox-through-Crabbox `tbx_01kwjsd175zx3727rf4v898cde`: `pnpm build` passed.\r\n- Enforcement dependency: `node scripts/check-dynamic-import-warts.mjs --fail-manual-memoizers` currently reports 174 remaining manual memoizers, with none in this PR's 37 owned paths; these are owned by the outstanding gateway/channel batches.\r\n- Fresh Codex autoreview: one valid sticky-rejection regression found and fixed; final rerun clean with no accepted/actionable findings, confidence 0.96.\r\n",
